IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc28-part26-extraordinary-remedies.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), sections 774 to 784 (PART XXVI, Extraordinary Remedies): certiorari, habeas corpus, mandamus, procedendo and prohibition
-- in criminal matters. Layer 1 of part ccc28.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified
-- against the official text.
-- READING A RESULT: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words (a failed "where" or "if" on a duty, a flat "no ... shall", a "means"); NOTHING where it is silent or limited by its own wording
-- (a named class, a list the text does not close, "by reason only", a named complement); the court's own judgments (in the opinion of the judge or court, considers proper) are inputs.
-- The five writs are an enum under this part's prefix, because the core has no type for them (NEEDS-CORE.md).

§ `The five writs of this Part`

-- "certiorari, habeas corpus, mandamus, procedendo and prohibition" (section 774).
DECLARE `s 774 writ` IS ONE OF
    `s 774 certiorari`
    `s 774 habeas corpus`
    `s 774 mandamus`
    `s 774 procedendo`
    `s 774 prohibition`
    `s 774 another writ`

§ `Part XXVI, section 774: application of the Part`

-- src:16621 | 774 This Part applies to proceedings in criminal matters by way of certiorari, habeas corpus, mandamus, procedendo and prohibition.
@ref s 774 (src:16621)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      writ IS A `s 774 writ`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 774 this Part applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings in a criminal matter`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings in criminal matters": the section speaks of criminal matters, and is silent about any other
    ELSE CONSIDER writ
         WHEN `s 774 certiorari` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 774 habeas corpus` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 774 mandamus` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 774 procedendo` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 774 prohibition` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 774 another writ` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the five writs are not closed with "only"

§ `Part XXVI, section 774.1: appearance in person on habeas corpus`

-- "Despite any other provision of this Act, the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus must appear in court in person."  The person is not among the core's `Party` constructors
-- (NEEDS-CORE.md): a party type of this section is declared here. The text states no time.
-- src:16623 | 774.1 Despite any other provision of this Act, the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus must appear in court in person.
@ref s 774.1 (src:16623)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears in court in person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appears in court in person as they must` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus": the section speaks of that person, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `the person appears in court in person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must appear in court in person"

DECLARE `s 774.1 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus`

DECLARE `s 774.1 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 774.1 appear in court in person`

-- src:16623 | 774.1 Despite any other provision of this Act, the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus must appear in court in person.
@ref s 774.1 (src:16623)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 774.1 party` `s 774.1 action`
`s 774.1 the duty of the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus to appear in person` MEANS
    PARTY `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus`
    MUST `s 774.1 appear in court in person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus` BECAUSE "the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus did not appear in court in person"

§ `Part XXVI, section 775: detention on inquiry to determine the legality of imprisonment`

-- "Where proceedings to which this Part applies have been instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction, by or in respect of a person who is in custody by reason that he is charged with or has been convicted
-- of an offence, to have the legality of his imprisonment determined, the judge or court may, without determining the question, make an order for the further detention of that person and direct the judge, justice or
-- provincial court judge under whose warrant he is in custody, or any other judge, justice or provincial court judge, to take any proceedings, hear such evidence or do any other thing that, in the opinion of the judge or
-- court, will best further the ends of justice."  A power ("may") with a "where" gate (JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)).
DECLARE `s 775 course` IS ONE OF
    `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person`
    `s 775 direct a judge, justice or provincial court judge to take proceedings, hear evidence or do another thing that will best further the ends of justice`
    `s 775 a course the section does not name`

-- src:16625 | 775 Where proceedings to which this Part applies have been instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction, by or in respect of a person who is in custody by reason that he is charged with or has been convicted of an offence, to have the legality of his imprisonment determined, the judge or court may, without determining the question, make an order for the further detention of that person and direct the judge, justice or provincial court judge under whose warrant he is in custody, or any other judge, justice or provincial court judge, to take any proceedings, hear such evidence or do any other thing that, in the opinion of the judge or court, will best further the ends of justice.
@ref s 775 (src:16625)
GIVEN `proceedings to which this Part applies have been instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are by or in respect of a person who is in custody by reason that the person is charged with or has been convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are to have the legality of the person's imprisonment determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the judge or court the direction will best further the ends of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 775 course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 775 the judge or court may take this course without determining the question` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `proceedings to which this Part applies have been instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction`
            AND `the proceedings are by or in respect of a person who is in custody by reason that the person is charged with or has been convicted of an offence`
            AND `the proceedings are to have the legality of the person's imprisonment determined`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where proceedings to which this Part applies have been instituted before a judge or court having jurisdiction, by or in respect of a person who is in custody by reason that he is charged with or has been convicted of an offence, to have the legality of his imprisonment determined"
    ELSE CONSIDER course
         WHEN `s 775 make an order for the further detention of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 775 direct a judge, justice or provincial court judge to take proceedings, hear evidence or do another thing that will best further the ends of justice` THEN
             IF `in the opinion of the judge or court the direction will best further the ends of justice`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that, in the opinion of the judge or court, will best further the ends of justice": the power is to direct what the judge or court thinks best, and the section is silent about any other direction
         WHEN `s 775 a course the section does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two courses are not closed with "only"

§ `Part XXVI, section 776: where a conviction or order is not reviewable by certiorari`

-- "No conviction or order shall be removed by certiorari (a) where an appeal was taken, whether or not the appeal has been carried to a conclusion; or (b) where the defendant appeared and pleaded and the merits were
-- tried, and an appeal might have been taken, but the defendant did not appeal."  The answer asked is whether this section bars removal; a case outside (a) and (b) is not barred BY THIS SECTION (the section does not
-- say the conviction may then be removed).
-- src:16627 | 776 No conviction or order shall be removed by certiorari
-- src:16628 | (a) where an appeal was taken, whether or not the appeal has been carried to a conclusion; or
-- src:16629 | (b) where the defendant appeared and pleaded and the merits were tried, and an appeal might have been taken, but the defendant did not appeal.
@ref s 776 (src:16627-16629)
GIVEN `an appeal was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant appeared and pleaded and the merits were tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal might have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant did not appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` MEANS
    IF `an appeal was taken`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the defendant appeared and pleaded and the merits were tried` AND `an appeal might have been taken` AND `the defendant did not appeal`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No conviction or order shall be removed by certiorari": neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) holds, so this section does not bar removal

§ `Part XXVI, sections 777 and 778: conviction or order remediable`

-- 777(1) "No conviction, order or warrant for enforcing a conviction or order shall, on being removed by certiorari, be held to be invalid by reason of any irregularity, informality or insufficiency therein, where the
-- court before which or the judge before whom the question is raised, on perusal of the evidence, is satisfied (a) that an offence of the nature described in the conviction, order or warrant, as the case may be, was
-- committed, (b) that there was jurisdiction to make the conviction or order or issue the warrant, as the case may be, and (c) that the punishment imposed, if any, was not in excess of the punishment that might lawfully
-- have been imposed, but the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings in the manner that the court or judge considers proper that are conferred on a court to which an appeal might have been taken."
-- src:16631 | 777 (1) No conviction, order or warrant for enforcing a conviction or order shall, on being removed by certiorari, be held to be invalid by reason of any irregularity, informality or insufficiency therein, where the court before which or the judge before whom the question is raised, on perusal of the evidence, is satisfied
-- src:16632 | (a) that an offence of the nature described in the conviction, order or warrant, as the case may be, was committed,
-- src:16633 | (b) that there was jurisdiction to make the conviction or order or issue the warrant, as the case may be, and
-- src:16634 | (c) that the punishment imposed, if any, was not in excess of the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed,
-- src:16635 | but the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings in the manner that the court or judge considers proper that are conferred on a court to which an appeal might have been taken.
@ref s 777(1) (src:16631-16635)
GIVEN `the conviction, order or warrant has been removed by certiorari` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invalidity alleged is by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or judge is satisfied that an offence of the nature described was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or judge is satisfied that there was jurisdiction to make the conviction or order or issue the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a punishment was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or judge is satisfied that the punishment imposed was not in excess of the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conviction, order or warrant has been removed by certiorari`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on being removed by certiorari": the subsection speaks of a conviction, order or warrant so removed, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF NOT `the invalidity alleged is by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency in it`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason of any irregularity, informality or insufficiency therein": the subsection is silent about invalidity on any other ground
         ELSE IF     `the court or judge is satisfied that an offence of the nature described was committed`
                 AND `the court or judge is satisfied that there was jurisdiction to make the conviction or order or issue the warrant`
                 AND ((NOT `a punishment was imposed`) OR `the court or judge is satisfied that the punishment imposed was not in excess of the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the court before which or the judge before whom the question is raised, on perusal of the evidence, is satisfied (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..."

-- The last clause of subsection (1): "but the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings in the manner that the court or judge considers proper that are conferred on a court to which an
-- appeal might have been taken."  Which powers an appeal court has is in Part XXI, outside this range; the manner is the court's own judgment.
-- src:16635 | but the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings in the manner that the court or judge considers proper that are conferred on a court to which an appeal might have been taken.
@ref s 777(1) (src:16635)
GIVEN `the court or judge is dealing with a conviction, order or warrant removed by certiorari` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(1) the court or judge has the same powers to deal with the proceedings as a court to which an appeal might have been taken` MEANS
    IF `the court or judge is dealing with a conviction, order or warrant removed by certiorari`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- in the manner that the court or judge considers proper: the manner is the court's judgment, and the powers are those of Part XXI
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court or judge has the same powers": the clause is given for proceedings under subsection (1), and is silent about any other

-- (2) "Where, in proceedings to which subsection (1) applies, the court or judge is satisfied that a person was properly convicted of an offence but the punishment that was imposed is greater than the punishment that
-- might lawfully have been imposed, the court or judge (a) shall correct the sentence, (i) where the punishment is a fine, by imposing a fine that does not exceed the maximum fine that might lawfully have been imposed,
-- (ii) where the punishment is imprisonment, and the person has not served a term of imprisonment under the sentence that is equal to or greater than the term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed, by
-- imposing a term of imprisonment that does not exceed the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed, or (iii) where the punishment is a fine and imprisonment, by imposing a punishment in
-- accordance with subparagraph (i) or (ii), as the case requires; or (b) shall remit the matter to the convicting judge, justice or provincial court judge and direct him to impose a punishment that is not greater than
-- the punishment that may be lawfully imposed."
-- src:16637 | (2) Where, in proceedings to which subsection (1) applies, the court or judge is satisfied that a person was properly convicted of an offence but the punishment that was imposed is greater than the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed, the court or judge
@ref s 777(2) (src:16637)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or judge is satisfied that the person was properly convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment that was imposed is greater than the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(2) the court or judge shall correct the sentence or remit the matter` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which subsection (1) applies` AND `the court or judge is satisfied that the person was properly convicted of the offence` AND `the punishment that was imposed is greater than the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in proceedings to which subsection (1) applies, the court or judge is satisfied that a person was properly convicted of an offence but the punishment that was imposed is greater than the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed"

DECLARE `s 777(2)(a) kind of punishment` IS ONE OF
    `s 777(2)(a)(i) a fine`
    `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment`
    `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment`

-- Paragraph (a): the corrected punishment. The fine is in dollars; the terms of imprisonment are lengths of time (the core's `Length of time`). `the person has served` is the term served under the sentence.
-- Subparagraph (ii) applies only "and the person has not served a term ... equal to or greater than the term ... that might lawfully have been imposed": where the person has served that much, subparagraph (ii)
-- states no correction and the answer is NOTHING (silent).
-- src:16638 | (a) shall correct the sentence,
-- src:16639 | (i) where the punishment is a fine, by imposing a fine that does not exceed the maximum fine that might lawfully have been imposed,
-- src:16640 | (ii) where the punishment is imprisonment, and the person has not served a term of imprisonment under the sentence that is equal to or greater than the term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed, by imposing a term of imprisonment that does not exceed the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed, or
-- src:16641 | (iii) where the punishment is a fine and imprisonment, by imposing a punishment in accordance with subparagraph (i) or (ii), as the case requires; or
@ref s 777(2)(a) (src:16638-16641)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 777(2)(a) kind of punishment`
      `the fine imposed on the correction` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum fine that might lawfully have been imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment imposed on the correction` IS A `Length of time`
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed` IS A `Length of time`
      `the term of imprisonment the person has served under the sentence` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(2)(a) the corrected sentence is in accordance with this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 777(2)(a)(i) a fine` THEN `the fine is corrected`
    WHEN `s 777(2)(a)(ii) imprisonment` THEN `the imprisonment is corrected`
    WHEN `s 777(2)(a)(iii) a fine and imprisonment` THEN
        CONSIDER `the imprisonment is corrected`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subparagraph (ii) states no correction where the person has served a term equal to or greater than the maximum, and subparagraph (iii) sends the case to (i) or (ii)
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by imposing a punishment in accordance with subparagraph (i) or (ii), as the case requires"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the fine is corrected`
    WHERE
        `the fine is corrected` MEANS
            IF `the fine imposed on the correction` AT MOST `the maximum fine that might lawfully have been imposed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by imposing a fine that does not exceed the maximum fine that might lawfully have been imposed"
        `the imprisonment is corrected` MEANS
            IF `s 777(2) the length of time is at least` `the term of imprisonment the person has served under the sentence` `the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subparagraph (ii) applies where the person "has not served a term of imprisonment under the sentence that is equal to or greater than the term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed"; for a person who has, the subsection states no correction
            ELSE IF `s 777(2) the length of time is at least` `the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed` `the term of imprisonment imposed on the correction`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by imposing a term of imprisonment that does not exceed the maximum term of imprisonment that might lawfully have been imposed"

-- helper: a is at least b as lengths of time (months first, then days; "less a day" takes a day off). This is the same comparison as the helper in ccc28-part24-s752.l4, written again here so that this module
-- imports the core only.
GIVEN a IS A `Length of time`
      b IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 777(2) the length of time is at least` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (a's years TIMES 12) PLUS a's months GREATER THAN (b's years TIMES 12) PLUS b's months THEN TRUE
        IF (a's years TIMES 12) PLUS a's months LESS THAN (b's years TIMES 12) PLUS b's months THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE (a's days MINUS (IF a's `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)) AT LEAST (b's days MINUS (IF b's `less a day` THEN 1 ELSE 0))

-- Paragraph (b): the matter is remitted and the convicting judge is directed to impose a punishment "not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed". The check is on the fine and on the term.
-- src:16642 | (b) shall remit the matter to the convicting judge, justice or provincial court judge and direct him to impose a punishment that is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed.
@ref s 777(2)(b) (src:16642)
GIVEN `the fine imposed on remittal` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum fine that may be lawfully imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment imposed on remittal` IS A `Length of time`
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that may be lawfully imposed` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(2)(b) the punishment imposed on remittal is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed` MEANS
    IF `the fine imposed on remittal` AT MOST `the maximum fine that may be lawfully imposed` AND `s 777(2) the length of time is at least` `the maximum term of imprisonment that may be lawfully imposed` `the term of imprisonment imposed on remittal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to impose a punishment that is not greater than the punishment that may be lawfully imposed"

-- (3) "Where an adjudication is varied pursuant to subsection (1) or (2), the conviction and warrant of committal, if any, shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied."
DECLARE `s 777(3) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 777(3) the conviction`
    `s 777(3) a warrant of committal`
    `s 777(3) another document`

-- src:16644 | (3) Where an adjudication is varied pursuant to subsection (1) or (2), the conviction and warrant of committal, if any, shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied.
@ref s 777(3) (src:16644)
GIVEN `an adjudication is varied pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `s 777(3) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(3) the document shall be amended to conform to the adjudication as varied` MEANS
    IF NOT `an adjudication is varied pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an adjudication is varied pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)"
    ELSE CONSIDER document
         WHEN `s 777(3) the conviction` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(3) a warrant of committal` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(3) another document` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the conviction and warrant of committal, if any": the subsection names two documents, and is silent about any other

-- (4) "Any statement that appears in a conviction and is sufficient for the purpose of the conviction is sufficient for the purposes of an information, summons, order or warrant in which it appears in the proceedings."
DECLARE `s 777(4) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 777(4) an information`
    `s 777(4) a summons`
    `s 777(4) an order`
    `s 777(4) a warrant`
    `s 777(4) another document`

-- src:16646 | (4) Any statement that appears in a conviction and is sufficient for the purpose of the conviction is sufficient for the purposes of an information, summons, order or warrant in which it appears in the proceedings.
@ref s 777(4) (src:16646)
GIVEN `the statement appears in a conviction and is sufficient for the purpose of the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `s 777(4) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 777(4) the statement is sufficient for the purposes of the document` MEANS
    IF NOT `the statement appears in a conviction and is sufficient for the purpose of the conviction`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any statement that appears in a conviction and is sufficient for the purpose of the conviction": the subsection is silent about any other statement
    ELSE CONSIDER document
         WHEN `s 777(4) an information` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(4) a summons` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(4) an order` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(4) a warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 777(4) another document` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the four documents are not closed with "only"

-- 778 "Without restricting the generality of section 777, that section shall be deemed to apply where (a) the statement of the adjudication or of any other matter or thing is in the past tense instead of in the present
-- tense; (b) the punishment imposed is less than the punishment that might by law have been imposed for the offence that appears by the evidence to have been committed; or (c) there has been an omission to negative
-- circumstances, the existence of which would make the act complained of lawful, whether those circumstances are stated by way of exception or otherwise in the provision under which the offence is charged or are stated
-- in another provision."  The answer asked is whether THIS section deems section 777 to apply; the section opens "Without restricting the generality of section 777", so a case outside (a) to (c) is not deemed by this
-- section but section 777 may still apply of its own force (fork F13).
-- src:16648 | 778 Without restricting the generality of section 777, that section shall be deemed to apply where
-- src:16649 | (a) the statement of the adjudication or of any other matter or thing is in the past tense instead of in the present tense;
-- src:16650 | (b) the punishment imposed is less than the punishment that might by law have been imposed for the offence that appears by the evidence to have been committed; or
-- src:16651 | (c) there has been an omission to negative circumstances, the existence of which would make the act complained of lawful, whether those circumstances are stated by way of exception or otherwise in the provision under which the offence is charged or are stated in another provision.
@ref s 778 (src:16648-16651)
GIVEN `the statement of the adjudication or of any other matter or thing is in the past tense instead of in the present tense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment imposed is less than the punishment that might by law have been imposed for the offence that appears by the evidence to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been an omission to negative circumstances, the existence of which would make the act complained of lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 778 section 777 is deemed by this section to apply` MEANS
    IF     `the statement of the adjudication or of any other matter or thing is in the past tense instead of in the present tense`
        OR `the punishment imposed is less than the punishment that might by law have been imposed for the offence that appears by the evidence to have been committed`
        OR `there has been an omission to negative circumstances, the existence of which would make the act complained of lawful`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that section shall be deemed to apply where": none of paragraphs (a) to (c) holds

§ `Part XXVI, sections 779 to 783`

-- 779(1) "A court that has authority to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding on certiorari may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash any such conviction, order or other proceeding removed to the
-- court by certiorari shall be heard unless the defendant has entered into a recognizance with one or more sufficient sureties, before one or more justices of the territorial division in which the conviction or order was
-- made or before a judge or other officer, or has made a deposit to be prescribed with a condition that the defendant will prosecute the writ of certiorari at his own expense, without wilful delay, and, if ordered, will
-- pay to the person in whose favour the conviction, order or other proceeding is affirmed his full costs and charges to be taxed according to the practice of the court where the conviction, order or proceeding is
-- affirmed."  A power ("may") given to a named class of court (a court with authority to quash on certiorari): outside it the text is silent.
-- src:16653 | 779 (1) A court that has authority to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding on certiorari may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash any such conviction, order or other proceeding removed to the court by certiorari shall be heard unless the defendant has entered into a recognizance with one or more sufficient sureties, before one or more justices of the territorial division in which the conviction or order was made or before a judge or other officer, or has made a deposit to be prescribed with a condition that the defendant will prosecute the writ of certiorari at his own expense, without wilful delay, and, if ordered, will pay to the person in whose favour the conviction, order or other proceeding is affirmed his full costs and charges to be taxed according to the practice of the court where the conviction, order or proceeding is affirmed.
@ref s 779(1) (src:16653)
GIVEN `the court has authority to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding on certiorari` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(1) the court may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash shall be heard unless the defendant gives security` MEANS
    IF `the court has authority to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding on certiorari`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that has authority to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding on certiorari may prescribe": the power is given to a named class of court, and the subsection is silent about any other

-- Under a general order of that kind, the motion to quash is not heard unless the defendant has entered into a recognizance with sufficient sureties, or has made a deposit, on the condition the subsection states.
GIVEN `a general order of that kind has been prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has entered into a recognizance with one or more sufficient sureties before one or more justices of the territorial division in which the conviction or order was made or before a judge or other officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has made a deposit to be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recognizance or deposit is on the condition that the defendant will prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense, without wilful delay, and, if ordered, will pay the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(1) the motion to quash may not be heard under the general order` MEANS
    IF NOT `a general order of that kind has been prescribed`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may prescribe by general order that no motion to quash ... shall be heard unless": the bar exists only under such an order, and the subsection is silent about a motion where none is prescribed
    ELSE IF (`the defendant has entered into a recognizance with one or more sufficient sureties before one or more justices of the territorial division in which the conviction or order was made or before a judge or other officer` OR `the defendant has made a deposit to be prescribed`) AND `the recognizance or deposit is on the condition that the defendant will prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense, without wilful delay, and, if ordered, will pay the costs`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be heard unless the defendant has entered into a recognizance": the unless is met, so the bar does not apply
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "The provisions of Part XXV relating to forfeiture of an amount set out in a recognizance apply to a recognizance entered into under this section."
-- src:16655 | (2) The provisions of Part XXV relating to forfeiture of an amount set out in a recognizance apply to a recognizance entered into under this section.
@ref s 779(2) (src:16655)
GIVEN `the recognizance is entered into under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 779(2) the provisions of Part XXV relating to forfeiture of an amount set out in a recognizance apply` MEANS
    IF `the recognizance is entered into under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a recognizance entered into under this section": the subsection speaks of that recognizance, and is silent about any other

-- 780 "Where a motion to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding is refused, the order of the court refusing the application is sufficient authority for the clerk of the court forthwith to return the conviction,
-- order or proceeding to the court from which or the person from whom it was removed, and for proceedings to be taken with respect thereto for the enforcement thereof."
-- src:16657 | 780 Where a motion to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding is refused, the order of the court refusing the application is sufficient authority for the clerk of the court forthwith to return the conviction, order or proceeding to the court from which or the person from whom it was removed, and for proceedings to be taken with respect thereto for the enforcement thereof.
@ref s 780 (src:16657)
GIVEN `a motion to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 780 the order refusing the application is sufficient authority for the clerk of the court to return the conviction, order or proceeding` MEANS
    IF `a motion to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a motion to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding is refused, the order of the court refusing the application is sufficient authority"

-- 781(1) "No order, conviction or other proceeding shall be quashed or set aside, and no defendant shall be discharged, by reason only that evidence has not been given (a) of a proclamation or order of the Governor in
-- Council or the lieutenant governor in council; (b) of rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council under an Act of Parliament or by the lieutenant governor in council under an Act of the legislature of
-- the province; or (c) of the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province."
DECLARE `s 781 matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council`
    `s 781(1)(b) rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council`
    `s 781(1)(c) the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province`
    `s 781 another matter`

-- src:16659 | 781 (1) No order, conviction or other proceeding shall be quashed or set aside, and no defendant shall be discharged, by reason only that evidence has not been given
-- src:16660 | (a) of a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council;
-- src:16661 | (b) of rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council under an Act of Parliament or by the lieutenant governor in council under an Act of the legislature of the province; or
-- src:16662 | (c) of the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province.
@ref s 781(1) (src:16659-16662)
GIVEN `the ground is only that evidence has not been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 781 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 781(1) the order, conviction or other proceeding shall not be quashed or set aside, nor the defendant discharged, by reason of this want of evidence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the ground is only that evidence has not been given`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that evidence has not been given": where there is another ground, the subsection is silent
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 781(1)(b) rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 781(1)(c) the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 781 another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) to (c) are not closed with "only"

-- (2) "Proclamations, orders, rules, regulations and by-laws mentioned in subsection (1) and the publication thereof shall be judicially noticed."
-- src:16664 | (2) Proclamations, orders, rules, regulations and by-laws mentioned in subsection (1) and the publication thereof shall be judicially noticed.
@ref s 781(2) (src:16664)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 781 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 781(2) the matter shall be judicially noticed` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 781(1)(a) a proclamation or order of the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 781(1)(b) rules, regulations or by-laws made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 781(1)(c) the publication of a proclamation, order, rule, regulation or by-law in the Canada Gazette or in the official gazette for the province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 781 another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "mentioned in subsection (1)": the subsection names those matters, and is silent about any other

-- 782 "No warrant of committal shall, on certiorari or habeas corpus, be held to be void by reason only of any defect therein, where (a) it is alleged in the warrant that the defendant was convicted; and (b) there is a
-- valid conviction to sustain the warrant."
-- src:16666 | 782 No warrant of committal shall, on certiorari or habeas corpus, be held to be void by reason only of any defect therein, where
-- src:16667 | (a) it is alleged in the warrant that the defendant was convicted; and
-- src:16668 | (b) there is a valid conviction to sustain the warrant.
@ref s 782 (src:16666-16668)
GIVEN `the proceeding is on certiorari or habeas corpus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is only a defect in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged in the warrant that the defendant was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a valid conviction to sustain the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 782 the warrant of committal shall not be held to be void by reason of the defect` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceeding is on certiorari or habeas corpus` AND `the ground is only a defect in the warrant`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on certiorari or habeas corpus ... by reason only of any defect therein": the section is silent about any other proceeding or ground
    ELSE IF `it is alleged in the warrant that the defendant was convicted` AND `there is a valid conviction to sustain the warrant`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where (a) it is alleged in the warrant that the defendant was convicted; and (b) there is a valid conviction to sustain the warrant"

-- 783 "Where an application is made to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding made or held by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a justice on the ground that he exceeded his jurisdiction, the court
-- to which or the judge to whom the application is made may, in quashing the conviction, order or other proceeding, order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice or provincial court judge or against
-- any officer who acted under the conviction, order or other proceeding or under any warrant issued to enforce it."  A power ("may") with a "where" gate and an "in quashing" gate (JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)).
-- src:16670 | 783 Where an application is made to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding made or held by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a justice on the ground that he exceeded his jurisdiction, the court to which or the judge to whom the application is made may, in quashing the conviction, order or other proceeding, order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice or provincial court judge or against any officer who acted under the conviction, order or other proceeding or under any warrant issued to enforce it.
@ref s 783 (src:16670)
GIVEN `the application is made to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding made or held by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is that the judge or justice exceeded their jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or judge is quashing the conviction, order or other proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 783 the court or judge may order that no civil proceedings shall be taken against the justice, provincial court judge or officer` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is made to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding made or held by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a justice` AND `the ground is that the judge or justice exceeded their jurisdiction`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to quash a conviction, order or other proceeding made or held by a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX or a justice on the ground that he exceeded his jurisdiction"
    ELSE IF `the court or judge is quashing the conviction, order or other proceeding`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in quashing the conviction, order or other proceeding"

§ `Part XXVI, section 784: appeals`

-- (1) "An appeal lies to the court of appeal from a decision granting or refusing the relief sought in proceedings by way of mandamus, certiorari or prohibition."
DECLARE `s 784(1) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 784(1) a decision granting the relief sought`
    `s 784(1) a decision refusing the relief sought`
    `s 784(1) another decision`

-- src:16672 | 784 (1) An appeal lies to the court of appeal from a decision granting or refusing the relief sought in proceedings by way of mandamus, certiorari or prohibition.
@ref s 784(1) (src:16672)
GIVEN writ IS A `s 774 writ`
      decision IS A `s 784(1) decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(1) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER writ
    WHEN `s 774 mandamus` THEN `the decision is within the subsection`
    WHEN `s 774 certiorari` THEN `the decision is within the subsection`
    WHEN `s 774 prohibition` THEN `the decision is within the subsection`
    WHEN `s 774 habeas corpus` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings by way of mandamus, certiorari or prohibition": habeas corpus is not named in this subsection; subsections (3) to (5) deal with it
    WHEN `s 774 procedendo` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings by way of mandamus, certiorari or prohibition": procedendo is not named
    WHEN `s 774 another writ` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings by way of mandamus, certiorari or prohibition"
    WHERE
        `the decision is within the subsection` MEANS
            CONSIDER decision
            WHEN `s 784(1) a decision granting the relief sought` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 784(1) a decision refusing the relief sought` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 784(1) another decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from a decision granting or refusing the relief sought": the subsection names those decisions, and is silent about any other

-- (2) "Except as provided in this section, Part XXI applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to appeals under this section."
-- src:16674 | (2) Except as provided in this section, Part XXI applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to appeals under this section.
@ref s 784(2) (src:16674)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this section provides otherwise on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(2) Part XXI applies to the appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the appeal is an appeal under this section`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to appeals under this section"
    ELSE IF `this section provides otherwise on the matter`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided in this section"
         ELSE JUST TRUE   -- with such modifications as the circumstances require: the modifications are in Part XXI and in the circumstances, and the subsection does not state them

-- (3) "Where an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein, no application may again be made on the same grounds, whether to the same or to
-- another court or judge, unless fresh evidence is adduced, but an appeal from that refusal shall lie to the court of appeal, and where on the appeal the application is refused a further appeal shall lie to the Supreme
-- Court of Canada, with leave of that Court."  Three answers: whether the bar on a further application applies; whether an appeal lies to the court of appeal; whether a further appeal lies, with leave.
-- On the bar, an "unless" once met: the bar then does not apply (fork F14: JUST FALSE for the bar; the other reading is that the subsection is then silent).
-- src:16676 | (3) Where an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein, no application may again be made on the same grounds, whether to the same or to another court or judge, unless fresh evidence is adduced, but an appeal from that refusal shall lie to the court of appeal, and where on the appeal the application is refused a further appeal shall lie to the Supreme Court of Canada, with leave of that Court.
@ref s 784(3) (src:16676)
GIVEN `an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new application is made on the same grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fresh evidence is adduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein"
    ELSE IF NOT `the new application is made on the same grounds`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no application may again be made on the same grounds": the bar is limited to the same grounds, and the subsection is silent about an application on other grounds
         ELSE IF `fresh evidence is adduced`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless fresh evidence is adduced"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 784(3) (src:16676)
GIVEN `an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(3) an appeal lies to the court of appeal from the refusal` MEANS
    IF `an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction therein ... an appeal from that refusal shall lie to the court of appeal"

@ref s 784(3) (src:16676)
GIVEN `the application is refused on the appeal to the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(3) a further appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is refused on the appeal to the court of appeal`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where on the appeal the application is refused a further appeal shall lie to the Supreme Court of Canada"
    ELSE IF `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with leave of that Court": the appeal lies with leave, and the subsection does not say whether it lies without it

-- (4) "Where a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is granted by any judge, no appeal therefrom shall lie at the instance of any party including the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada."
-- src:16678 | (4) Where a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is granted by any judge, no appeal therefrom shall lie at the instance of any party including the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 784(4) (src:16678)
GIVEN `a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is granted by a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(4) an appeal lies from the granting of the writ` MEANS
    IF `a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is granted by a judge`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no appeal therefrom shall lie at the instance of any party including the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is granted by any judge": the subsection is silent where it is not granted

-- (5) "Where a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum, an appeal therefrom lies to the court of appeal, and from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, with the
-- leave of that Court, at the instance of the applicant or the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada, but not at the instance of any other party."
DECLARE `s 784(5) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 784(5) the applicant`
    `s 784(5) the Attorney General of the province concerned`
    `s 784(5) the Attorney General of Canada`
    `s 784(5) any other party`

DECLARE `s 784(5) appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal`
    `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada`

-- src:16680 | (5) Where a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum, an appeal therefrom lies to the court of appeal, and from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, with the leave of that Court, at the instance of the applicant or the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada, but not at the instance of any other party.
@ref s 784(5) (src:16680)
GIVEN `a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum` IS A BOOLEAN
      appeal IS A `s 784(5) appeal`
      appellant IS A `s 784(5) appellant`
      `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` MEANS
    IF NOT `a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum, an appeal therefrom lies"
    ELSE CONSIDER appellant
         WHEN `s 784(5) any other party` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not at the instance of any other party"
         WHEN `s 784(5) the applicant` THEN `the appeal lies`
         WHEN `s 784(5) the Attorney General of the province concerned` THEN `the appeal lies`
         WHEN `s 784(5) the Attorney General of Canada` THEN `the appeal lies`
    WHERE
        `the appeal lies` MEANS
            CONSIDER appeal
            WHEN `s 784(5) an appeal to the court of appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 784(5) an appeal from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` THEN
                IF `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the Supreme Court of Canada, with the leave of that Court": the appeal lies with leave, and the subsection does not say whether it lies without it

-- (6) "An appeal in habeas corpus matters shall be heard by the court to which the appeal is directed at an early date, whether in or out of the prescribed sessions of the court."  "At an early date" is open-textured and is
-- not computed (fork F1): whether the appeal was heard at an early date is the court's judgment and is taken as an input; the sessions do not matter.
-- src:16682 | (6) An appeal in habeas corpus matters shall be heard by the court to which the appeal is directed at an early date, whether in or out of the prescribed sessions of the court.
@ref s 784(6) (src:16682)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal in a habeas corpus matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is heard at an early date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 784(6) the appeal is heard at an early date as it shall be` MEANS
    IF NOT `the appeal is an appeal in a habeas corpus matter`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal in habeas corpus matters": the subsection speaks of those appeals, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `the appeal is heard at an early date`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be heard by the court to which the appeal is directed at an early date"

DECLARE `s 784(6) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 784(6) hear the appeal at an early date`

-- src:16682 | (6) An appeal in habeas corpus matters shall be heard by the court to which the appeal is directed at an early date, whether in or out of the prescribed sessions of the court.
@ref s 784(6) (src:16682)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 784(6) action`
`s 784(6) the court's duty to hear the appeal in a habeas corpus matter at an early date` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 784(6) hear the appeal at an early date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court to which the appeal is directed did not hear the appeal in a habeas corpus matter at an early date"
